 RSSI in dBm (noise isn't used in AM) and `tone_ok = true`. `tx()` is never called while AM is on. NULL = no AM.
 On an FD6818 `rx_am` is `rx` plus the AF output type AM (`fd6818_set_am`, 0x47 = 0x0740; inferred, section 2);
 `rx()` and `set_mode()` write FM back.
+
+The derivative's receive-gain candidate keeps this AF and filter setup. On a receiver using `fd6818_am_status`,
+the gain ceiling is the word read before entering AM; unknown words disable gain changes. Each status poll reduces
+gain above raw RSSI 143, holds it in the target band, and recovers one table entry per poll below 130 after a
+30-poll hold. Gain changes discard the previous RSSI sample. The board adds the attenuation at the sample's gain
+back to RSSI before the core's existing AM squelch mapping. Each AM tune resets to the saved ceiling; leaving AM
+restores it. The board skips gain updates during receiver sleep or transmit. Physical audio validation is pending.
 
